\section*{6-2 \quad THE ENERGY SPECTRUM OF THE HARMONIC OSCILLATOR}

The Hamiltonian for the harmonic oscillator has the form

\begin{equation}
H = \frac{p^2}{2m} + \frac{1}{2} m\omega^2 x^2
\tag{6-33}
\end{equation}

where $x$ and $p$ are operators. The only properties of these operators that we shall use are that they are hermitian and that they obey the commutation relations

\begin{equation}
[p, x] = -i\hbar
\tag{6-34}
\end{equation}

Classically the Hamiltonian could be factored into

\begin{equation*}
H = \omega \left( \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2}} x - i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega}} \right) \! \left( \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2}} x + i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega}} \right)
\end{equation*}

but because $x$ and $p$ do not commute, we have

\begin{align}
\omega \left( \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2}} x - i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega}} \right) \! \left( \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2}} x + i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega}} \right) &= \frac{p^2}{2m} + \frac{m\omega^2}{2} x^2 - \frac{i\omega}{2} (px - xp) \nonumber \\
&= H - \frac{1}{2} \hbar\omega
\tag{6-35}
\end{align}

We now introduce a special notation for the operators in terms of which $H - \frac{1}{2} \hbar\omega$ is factored. We write

\begin{align}
A &= \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}} x + i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega\hbar}} \nonumber \\
A^\dagger &= \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}} x - i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega\hbar}}
\tag{6-36}
\end{align}

with the additional factor $\sqrt{1/\hbar}$ introduced to make $A$ and $A^\dagger$ dimensionless. Since $x$ and $p$ are hermitian, $A^\dagger$ is indeed the hermitian conjugate of $A$. We compute

\begin{equation}
[A, A^\dagger] = \left[ \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}} x , - i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega\hbar}} \right] + \left[ i \frac{p}{\sqrt{2m\omega\hbar}} , \sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}} x \right] = 1
\tag{6-37}
\end{equation}",
