\begin{equation*}
l_2|u\rangle = L_y|u\rangle = \frac{1}{i\hbar}[L_z, L_x]|u\rangle = \frac{1}{i\hbar}L_z l_1|u\rangle = 0
\end{equation*}

Similarly, we can show that $l_1|u\rangle = 0$. This means that only for $\mathbf{L} = 0$ can we have simul
