We thus will deal with simultaneous eigenfunctions of $\mathbf{L}^2$ and $L_z$. We will denote the
eigenkets by $|l, m\rangle$. Our starting point is thus the set of equations

\begin{equation*}
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{L}^2|l, m\rangle &= \hbar^2 l(l + 1)|l, m\rangle \\
L_z|l, m\rangle &= \hbar m|l, m\rangle
\end{aligned}
\tag{7-8}
\end{equation*}

