\tag{11-17}
\end{equation}
subject to the hermiticity requirement that $h_{ij} = h_{ji}^*$.

We can now separate the problem into two parts. First, we diagonalize the upper left corner $2\times2$ matrix. As noted in Chapter 9, a hermitian matrix $H$ will be diagonalized by a unitary transformation $U$:
$$UHU^{\dagger} = H_D$$
