\begin{equation}
U = \begin{pmatrix} \times & \times & 0 \\ \times & \times & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
\tag{11-18}
\end{equation}
where the $\times$'s denote unknown $U_{ij}$. The important thing is to note that this $U$ will not affect $H_0$: The lower right-hand corner is multiplied by 1. The upper $2\times2$ left corner of $H_0$ is of the form $E^{(0)} \times \mathbf{1}$ where $\mathbf{1}$ is the $2\times2$ unit matrix. As a consequence of $U \mathbf{1} U^{\dagger} = \mathbf{1}$, that corner is also unchanged. The net effect of the diagonalization is thus to diagonalize the $2\times2$ matrix
